1436 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The BFS algorithm starts by adding the initial state to the Statespace V and Queue D, an ordered set of states replacing the search stack employed in DFS.  It follows a FIFO policy, iteratively dequeuing a state s from the head, processing its transitions in \(A.T\), and enqueuing unvisited successor states \(s'\) to the tail.  The search continues until the queue is empty, building V with all reachable states while exploring the state space level-by-level.)
/E (The BFS algorithm starts by adding the initial state to the Statespace V and Queue D, an ordered set of states replacing the search stack employed in DFS.  It follows a FIFO policy, iteratively dequeuing a state s from the head, processing its transitions in \(A.T\), and enqueuing unvisited successor states \(s'\) to the tail.  The search continues until the queue is empty, building V with all reachable states while exploring the state space level-by-level.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
